# Conventional Commits

Use [Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/) for **every** suggested or drafted commit message and PR title.

## Format

```text
<type>(<optional-scope>): <short imperative description>
```

- **Type** is required; **scope** is optional but preferred when it clarifies the area (`api`, `ui`, `config`, `deps`, `ci`, `docs`).
- Description: imperative mood, lowercase after the colon, no trailing period, ~72 chars or less for the subject line.

## Allowed types (use the closest fit)

| Type | Use for |
|------|---------|
| `feat` | New user-visible behavior or capability |
| `fix` | Bug fixes |
| `refactor` | Internal change without intended behavior change |
| `perf` | Performance improvements |
| `test` | Tests only |
| `docs` | Documentation only |
| `chore` | Maintenance, tooling, ignores, formatting unrelated to product logic |
| `build` | Build system or packaging |
| `ci` | CI configuration |

## Examples

```text
feat(api): add pagination to list endpoints
fix(auth): reject expired refresh tokens
refactor(ui): extract shared form validation
docs(readme): document local setup commands
chore(deps): bump lint tooling
```

## Do not

- Use vague subjects (`update`, `fix stuff`, `changes`).
- Omit the type prefix for commits or PR titles you propose.
- Add `Co-authored-by`, `generated-by`, or assistant attribution trailers to commit messages.
